I need to prove:
- ClientA: `F.Large((s + t) + u, k)` given `F.Size(s) > k`
- ClientB: `F.Large(s + (t + u), k)` given `F.Size(t) > k`

For ClientA using ViewA (has ConcatA, Finish):
- Need `Size((s+t)+u) > k`
- `ConcatA(s+t, u)` gives `Size((s+t)+u) == Size(s+t) + Size(u)`
- `ConcatA(s, t)` gives `Size(s+t) == Size(s) + Size(t)`
- Since `Size(s) > k`, we have `Size(s+t) + Size(u) >= Size(s) > k`
- Then `Finish((s+t)+u, k)`

For ClientB using ViewB (has ConcatB, Finish):
- Need `Size(s+(t+u)) > k`
- `ConcatB(s, t+u)` gives `Size(s+(t+u)) == Size(s) + Size(t+u)`
- `ConcatB(t, u)` gives `Size(t+u) == Size(t) + Size(u)`
- Since `Size(t) > k`, we have `Size(s) + Size(t+u) >= Size(t) > k`
- Then `Finish(s+(t+u), k)`

{"ClientA.dfy":"include "Facts.dfy"
module ClientA {
  import F = Facts`ViewA
  lemma Prove(s: seq<int>, t: seq<int>, u: seq<int>, k: nat)
    requires F.Size(s) > k
    ensures F.Large((s + t) + u, k)
  {
    F.ConcatA(s, t);
    F.ConcatA(s + t, u);
    F.Finish((s + t) + u, k);
  }
}
","ClientB.dfy":"include "Facts.dfy"
module ClientB {
  import F = Facts`ViewB
  lemma Prove(s: seq<int>, t: seq<int>, u: seq<int>, k: nat)
    requires F.Size(t) > k
    ensures F.Large(s + (t + u), k)
  {
    F.ConcatB(t, u);
    F.ConcatB(s, t + u);
    F.Finish(s + (t + u), k);
  }
}
"}

